        "title": "Peace Without Security",
        "body": "The Moscow Peace Treaty ended the Winter War but left Finland wounded and anxious. Karelia had been ceded, hundreds of thousands were displaced, and many Finns feared the Soviet Union would return to finish what it had started.\n\nDrifting Toward Germany: Britain and France were unable to guarantee Finnish security, while the Soviet threat remained close. Finland gradually accepted military cooperation and transit arrangements with Germany, a dangerous alignment born from fear and strategic isolation.",
