      {
        "title": "Germany Invades the Soviet Union",
        "body": "On 22 June 1941, Germany launched Operation Barbarossa. Finland allowed German forces to operate from its territory, and Soviet aircraft bombed Finnish cities days later. Finland declared that it was again at war with the Soviet Union.\n\nCo-Belligerent, Not Axis Member: Finland fought alongside Germany against the Soviet Union but did not sign the Tripartite Pact. Finnish leaders described the war as a limited struggle to regain lost territory and secure the state, though cooperation with Nazi Germany deeply shaped the conflict.",
        "img": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Operation_Barbarossa_map.svg",
        "cap": "Operation Barbarossa opened a vast new front against the Soviet Union",
        "stats": [
