      {
        "title": "The Army Moves East",
        "body": "Finnish forces attacked across the old border and rapidly retook much of the territory lost in 1940. For many soldiers and evacuees, the campaign felt like a recovery of stolen homes rather than a war of conquest.\n\nBeyond the Old Border: Finland also advanced into East Karelia beyond the 1939 border, raising difficult questions about war aims. Some saw a chance to build a Greater Finland; others worried that moving too far tied Finland more tightly to Germany's war.",
        "img": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Finnish_advance_in_Karelia_1941_map.svg",
