        "title": "A City Under Siege",
        "body": "Germany encircled Leningrad from the south while Finnish forces held positions to the north. Finland did not launch a major assault into the city, but its presence helped close the ring around one of the war's most catastrophic sieges.\n\nLimited War Aims Tested: Finnish leaders tried to balance military cooperation with Germany against their own limited goals. Refusing a direct assault on Leningrad preserved some independence of action, but Finland remained tied to a brutal Axis campaign in the east.",
