        "body": "In East Karelia, Finland established military rule over territory that had not belonged to independent Finland. Officials treated Finnic populations differently from Russians, reflecting ethnic nationalist ideas that shaped occupation policy.\n\nCamps and Hardship: Thousands of civilians were held in camps during the occupation, and many suffered from hunger, disease, and forced displacement. The occupation remains one of the darkest parts of Finland's wartime history.",
