    "slides": [
      {
        "title": "War of Positions",
        "body": "After the 1941 advances, the front became largely static. Soldiers built trenches, bunkers, and supply lines through forest and swamp. The war did not stop, but it settled into patrols, artillery, raids, and waiting.\n\nA Country Under Strain: Finland's home front lived with rationing, air raids, displaced families, and dependence on German food and arms. The longer the war lasted, the harder it became to believe Germany would win or that Finland could escape the consequences easily.",
        "img": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Finnish_trench_Continuation_War.jpg",
